# Written by `aso install` from aso.toml ([air] public_name, public_cert,
# public_key, ws_addr). Don't edit: change aso.toml and run `aso install` again.
# Where this file is written is [air] nginx_conf: point it into the folder your
# nginx reads its sites from (for example /etc/nginx/conf.d/ on Linux, or
# /opt/homebrew/etc/nginx/servers/ on macOS with Homebrew). `aso install` checks
# it with `nginx -t` when nginx is installed; reloading nginx is yours to do,
# because nginx is shared with whatever else the machine serves.
#
# nginx answers on {{public_name}} and forwards the WebSocket to air_server,
# which listens on {{ws_addr}} on this machine. fsp-mint and the service's
# ecash-wallet reach air_server directly on this machine and do not go through
# nginx.
